    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scaenārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the stage</i>, <i>scenic</i>, <i>dramatic</i>, <i>theatrical</i> (late Lat. for scaenicus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artifices,</span>”
				i. e. <i>players</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 4, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">PICTOR,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a scenepainter</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. 948, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
